$\begin{align}
0.2^4 &= 0.2 \cdot 0.2 \cdot 0.2 \cdot 0.2
\\\\
&=0.0016
\end{align}$

Since $0.2$ is two tenths, we can use fractions instead:

$\begin{align}
0.2^4 &= \dfrac{2}{10} \cdot \dfrac{2}{10} \cdot \dfrac{2}{10} \cdot \dfrac{2}{10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2}{10 \cdot 10 \cdot 10 \cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{16}{10{,}000}
\\\\
&=0.0016 &&\gray{\text{(Sixteen ten-thousandths)}}
\end{align}$
